# L §4.6 step 3: "prefer in turn: 1. inside a scenario, the row from the higher layer (§6.4); 2. the narrower row".
# In sc, the scenario's x[1..5] beats the base's narrower x[3] at key 3, since step 3.1 comes first; in the base only
# x[3] is a candidate.
=== base.tally
model base
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2028-12-31

source s "s"

index ns = 1..10
input x[n in ns]: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  x[3] = 1

ask qb: x[3] law 2027-06-01
=== sc.tally
scenario sc over base
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version w
  cite s
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-06-01
  x[1..5] = 2

ask qs: x[3] in sc law 2027-06-01
ask qs4: x[4] in sc law 2027-06-01
=== expect
qb: 1
...
qs: 2
  world: sc
...
